t looks easily separable.`\\n    : `The background should be fully opaque (100% opacity).`;\\n\\n  const prompt \u003d `\\n    Transform the person in this photo into a professional high-quality headshot. \\n    Style Instruction: ${stylePrompt}.\\n    Backdrop Instruction: ${opacityInstruction}.\\n    Important: Keep the person\u0027s facial features, hair, and identity consistent with the source image. \\n    Ensure the output is a single, clear, front-facing portrait suitable for LinkedIn or a corporate website.\\n  `;\\n\\n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\\n    model: MODELS.IMAGE_GEN,\\n    contents: {\\n      parts: [\\n        {\\n          inlineData: {\\n            data: base64Image,\\n            mimeType: \u0027image/png\u0027,\\n          },\\n        },\\n        { text: prompt },\\n      ],\\n    },\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const part of response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts || []) {\\n    if (part.inlineData) {\\n      return `data:image/png;base64,${part.inlineData.data}`;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  throw new Error(\\\"No image data returned from Gemini\\\");\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Edits an existing image based on a natural language text prompt\\n */\\nexport const editHeadshot \u003d async (base64Image: string, editPrompt: string): Promise\u003cstring\u003e \u003d\u003e {\\n  const ai \u003d getAI();\\n  const prompt \u003d `\\n    Apply the following edit to this headshot: \\\"${editPrompt}\\\".\\n    Preserve the subject\u0027s identity and the professional quality of the photo.\\n  `;\\n\\n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\\n    model: MODELS.IMAGE_GEN,\\n    contents: {\\n      parts: [\\n        {\\n          inlineData: {\\n            data: base64Image.includes(\u0027,\u0027) ? base64Image.split(\u0027,\u0027)[1] : base64Image,\\n            mimeType: \u0027image/png\u0027,\\n          },\\n        },\\n        { text: prompt },\\n      ],\\n    },\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const part of response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts || []) {\\n    if (part.inlineData) {\\n      return `data:image/png;base64,${part.inlineData.data}`;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  throw new Error(\\\"No image data returned from Gemini\\\");\\n};\\n\"}]}]},\"createdTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1770118243,\"nanos\":349000000},\"doneTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1770118297,\"nanos\":28000000}},{\"id\":12,\"author\":\"user\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Implement undo and redo functionality for edits made in the \u0027Smart AI Editor\u0027, allowing users to revert or reapply changes.\",\"files\":[],\"fileUploads\":[],\"cMarkNode\":{}},\"createdTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1770118315,\"nanos\":331000000}},{\"id\":13,\"author\":\"model\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"text\":\"**Examining State Management**\\n\\nI\u0027m currently analyzing the state management within `App.tsx`, specifically focusing on how `currentImage` and `history` are handled. My initial assessment indicates that these variables present a solid foundation for implementing undo/redo functionality, provided their use is comprehensive. I\u0027m thinking I can build upon these variables for the history of image states, to allow reversal.\\n\\n\\n**Developing Undo/Redo Logic**\\n\\nI\u0027m now focusing on implementing undo/redo functionality using a pointer within the existing `history` array. My plan involves `historyIndex` management, clearing the \\\"redo\\\" chain on new edits, and updating `currentImage` in sync with changes to the `historyIndex`. I\u0027m starting the refactor of `App.tsx` and intend to add \\\"Undo\\\" and \\\"Redo\\\" buttons to the UI. I have to flip the order of the history.\\n\\n\\n\",\"cMarkNode\":{}},\"createdTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1770118315,\"nanos\":332000000},\"doneTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1770118324,\"nanos\":540000000}},{\"id\":14,\"author\":\"model\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"generationTable\",\"entries\":[{\"path\":\"App.tsx\",\"generationType\":1,\"isDone\":true,\"description\":\"Implemented undo 