1000000}},{\"id\":19,\"author\":\"model\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"text\":\"**Implementing Local Storage**\\n\\nI\u0027m currently focused on integrating `localStorage` into the ProShot AI application. The goal is to ensure data persistence, specifically for the image history, index, the original image, and the selected style. I\u0027m prioritizing saving these states upon any change, and loading them upon initial application startup.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Persistence Strategy**\\n\\nI\u0027m now refining the `useEffect` hooks in `App.tsx` for data persistence. My focus is on ensuring all application variations and the current selection are saved to `localStorage`. I\u0027m going to include `history`, `historyIndex`, `originalImage`, `selectedStyle`, and `bgOpacity` in the dependency array. My current roadblock is the large size of `originalImage`, which is a base64 string.\\n\\n\\n**Addressing Storage Limits**\\n\\nI\u0027ve hit a snag with `localStorage`: the image history, with its base64 strings, could easily exceed the storage limit (around 5MB). I\u0027m implementing the requested history persistence for now, but I\u0027ll add a `try-catch` to handle potential quota errors. I\u0027m also considering only saving a limited number of the most recent images. I\u0027ve updated my state management to initialize from `localStorage` on component mount. The code I am writing includes `STORAGE_KEY \u003d \u0027proshot_ai_state\u0027` to be used in the component.\\n\\n\\n**Finalizing Initialization Logic**\\n\\nMy focus is now on solidifying the initialization logic from `localStorage`. I\u0027ve added a robust `try-catch` block during component mount to handle potential parsing errors from the stored JSON string, logging any failures. I\u0027m carefully initializing state variables like history and the selected style from the saved data. I\u0027m also implementing a `useEffect` hook to ensure state is saved whenever it changes.\\n\\n\\n**Optimizing Persistence Updates**\\n\\nI\u0027m now refining the persistence strategy within the `useEffect` hook, to improve efficiency. I\u0027m taking a closer look at `localStorage.setItem` and considering how frequently it\u0027s called with the history changing, which could become a performance bottleneck. The \\\"reset\\\" functionality will also be expanded to clear `localStorage`. I will ensure that the loading `useEffect` only runs once to avoid double-mounts caused by `React.StrictMode`. The persistence logic is being added to `App.tsx`, and I\u0027m deciding whether to store the `selectedStyle` id or the whole object. I\u0027ll need to figure this out before deployment.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Data Initialization**\\n\\nI\u0027m now integrating more robust initialization of state variables. I\u0027ve updated the `useState` hooks for `originalImage`, `bgOpacity`, and `history` to handle scenarios where saved data is missing or corrupted within `localStorage`. I have added error handling for parsing the JSON, defaulting to the initial state values when parsing fails, and will ensure that the initial data defaults correctly. I\u0027ve also implemented a function to ensure that a style defaults properly as well.\\n\\n\\n**Enhancing State Management**\\n\\nMy focus is now on improving the state management surrounding `localStorage`, particularly concerning the `Undo/Redo` functionality. I am also planning to modify the reset function to also clear `localStorage` after an undo/redo action. I am thinking I can do this using the `useEffect` hook. I\u0027m also addressing the potential failures of `localStorage` in private browsing or due to a storage quota.\\n\\n\\n\",\"cMarkNode\":{}},\"createdTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1771236848,\"nanos\":81000000},\"doneTimestamp\":{\"seconds\":1771236869,\"nanos\":950000000}},{\"id\":20,\"author\":\"model\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"generationTable\",\"entries\":[{\"path\":\"App.tsx\",\"generationType\":1,\"isDone\":true,\"description\":\"Implemented localStorage persistence to automatically save and load user project state, including generation history, original image, and current selections. Added specialized initialization logic for state variables and an auto-save effect.\",\"diffs\":[{\"target\":\"\",\"replacement\":\"\\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\\nimport { Layout } from \u0027./components/Layout\u0027;\\nimport { StyleCard } from \u0027./components/StyleCard\u0027;\\nimport { HEADSHOT_STYLES } from \u0027./constants\u0027;\\nimport { HeadshotStyle, ProcessingState, ImageRecord } from \u0027./types\u0027;\\nimport { fileToBase64, generateHeadshot, editHeadshot } from \u0027./services/gemini\u0027;\\n\\nconst STORAGE_KEY \u003d \u0027proshot_ai_session_data\u0027;\\n\\nconst App: React.FC \u003d () \u003d\u003e {\\n  // Initialize state from localStorage with fallback to defaults\\n  const [selectedStyle, setSelectedStyle] \u003d useState\u003cHeadshotStyle\u003e(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\\n    if (saved) {\\n      try {\\n        const parsed \u003d JSON.parse(saved);\\n        const style \u003d HEADSHOT_STYLES.find(s \u003d\u003e s.id \u003d\u003d\u003d parsed.selectedStyleId);\\n        return style || HEADSHOT_STYLES[0];\\n      } catch (e) { return HEADSHOT_STYLES[0]; }\\n    }\\n    return HEADSHOT_STYLES[0];\\n  });\\n\\n  const [bgOpacity, setBgOpacity] \u003d useState\u003cnumber\u003e(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\\n    if (saved) {\\n      try { return JSON.parse(saved).bgOpacity ?? 100; } catch (e) { return 100; }\\n    }\\n    return 100;\\n  });\\n\\n  const [originalImage, setOriginalImage] \u003d useState\u003cstring | null\u003e(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\\n    if (saved) {\\n      try { return JSON.parse(saved).originalImage || null; } catch (e) { return null; }\\n    }\\n    return null;\\n  });\\n\\n  const [history, setHistory] \u003d useState\u003cImageRecord[]\u003e(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\\n    if (saved) {\\n      try { return JSON.parse(saved).history || []; } catch (e) { return []; }\\n    }\\n    return [];\\n  });\\n\\n  const [historyIndex, setHistoryIndex] \u003d useState\u003cnumber\u003e(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\\n    if (saved) {\\n      try { return JSON.parse(saved).historyIndex ?? -1; } catch (e) { return -1; }\\n    }\\n    return -1;\\n  });\\n\\n  const [processing, setProcessing] \u003d useState\u003cProcessingState\u003e({ status: \u0027idle\u0027 });\\n  const [editPrompt, setEditPrompt] \u003d useState(\u0027\u0027);\\n\\n  const fileInputRef \u003d useRef\u003cHTMLInputElement\u003e(null);\\n\\n  // Persistence Effect: Automatically save state whenever critical data changes\\n  useEffect(() \u003d\u003e {\\n    const data \u003d {\\n      selectedStyleId: selectedStyle.id,\\n      bgOpacity,\\n      originalImage,\\n      history,\\n      historyIndex,\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      // If quota exceeded, we log it but don\u0027t crash. \\n      // This can happen with many high-res base64 images in localStorage.\\n      console.warn(\\\"LocalStorage quota exceeded. Your full history might not be saved.\\\", e);\\n    }\\n  }, [selectedStyle, bgOpacity, originalImage, history, historyIndex]);\\n\\n  // Derived state: current image is based on history and historyIndex\\n  const currentImage \u003d historyIndex \u003e\u003d 0 ? history[historyIndex] : null;\\n\\n  const addToHistory \u003d (record: ImageRecord) \u003d\u003e {\\n    // If we are currently in an \\\"undone\\\" state, we clear the \\\"redo\\\" portion\\n    // when a new action is performed.\\n    const newHistory \u003d [record, ...history.slice(historyIndex \u003d\u003d\u003d -1 ? 0 : historyIndex)];\\n    setHistory(newHistory);\\n    setHistoryIndex(0);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleFileChange \u003d async (e: React.ChangeEvent\u003cHTMLInputElement\u003e) \u003d\u003e {\\n    const file \u003d e.target.files?.[0];\\n    if (file) {\\n      try {\\n        setProcessing({ status: \u0027loading\u0027, message: \u0027Analyzing your selfie...\u0027 });\\n        const base64 \u003d await fileToBase64(file);\\n        const dataUrl \u003d `data:image/png;base64,${base64}`;\\n        setOriginalImage(dataUrl);\\n        const newRecord: ImageRecord \u003d {\\n          id: Date.now().toString(),\\n          url: dataUrl,\\n          type: \u0027original\u0027,\\n          timestamp: Date.now()\\n        };\\n        setHistory([newRecord]);\\n        setHistoryIndex(0);\\n        setProcessing({ status: \u0027idle\u0027 });\\n      } catch (err) {\\n        setProcessing({ status: \u0027error\u0027, message: \u0027Failed to read file. Try another photo.\u0027 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleGenerate \u003d async () \u003d\u003e {\\n    if (!originalImage) return;\\n\\n    setProcessing({ status: \u0027loading\u0027, message: `Crafting your ${selectedStyle.name} headshot...` });\\n    try {\\n      const base64 \u003d originalImage.split(\u0027,\u0027)[1];\\n      const resultUrl \u003d await generateHeadshot(base64, selectedStyle.prompt, bgOpacity);\\n      const newRecord: ImageRecord \u003d {\\n        id: Date.now().toString(),\\n        url: resultUrl,\\n        type: \u0027generated\u0027,\\n        timestamp: Date.now()\\n      };\\n      addToHistory(newRecord);\\n      setProcessing({ status: \u0027success\u0027 });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      console.error(err);\\n      setProcessing({ status: \u0027error\u0027, message: \u0027AI generation failed. Please try again.\u0027 });\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleEdit \u003d async (customPrompt?: string) \u003d\u003e {\\n    const promptToUse \u003d customPrompt || editPrompt;\\n    